class:: GbmanSonify
summary:: Explicit Gingerbreadman-map clock and level sonifier
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/GbmanMap, Classes/HenonSonify

description::

This explicit sonifier drives the piecewise-linear Gingerbreadman map at audio rates. Because the underlying map jumps abruptly through absolute-value transformations, the resulting audio signal is highly discontinuous and jagged. By safely wrapping and scaling these exploding coordinates, this UGen produces harsh, digital, erratic textures and screaming alias-heavy tones, useful for industrial sound design and glitch synthesis.

Uses link::Classes/GbmanMap::'s recurrence, explicitly folding selected coordinates into iteration frequency and bipolar level. Frequency is bounded to the audio sample rate and the scheduler retains phase remainder.

Interpolation is hold, linear, or cubic Hermite. Unlike GbmanMap, this class intentionally maps state to sound.

subsection:: Visualizing the internal dynamics

See link::Classes/GbmanMap:: for the recurrence's static portrait and exact-state live view. The sonifier does not expose its internal coordinates, so a separately instantiated map would be illustrative but not synchronized to its audio orbit.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: minFreq
Mapped minimum iteration hertz.
argument:: maxFreq
Mapped maximum iteration hertz.
argument:: clockLo
Lower clock-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: clockHi
Upper clock-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: outputLo
Lower level-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: outputHi
Upper level-coordinate folding bound.
argument:: clockIndex
Init-rate clock coordinate: 0 x, 1 y.
argument:: outputIndex
Init-rate level coordinate: 0 x, 1 y.
argument:: interp
Init-rate 0 hold, 1 linear, 2 cubic Hermite.
argument:: x0
Initial x state.
argument:: y0
Initial y state.
argument:: reset
Restore map, phase, and interpolation state.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ GbmanSonify.ar * 0.05 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ GbmanSonify.ar(30, 4000, interp: 1) * 0.05 }.play
)
::

code::
// Piecewise Industrial Screamer
(
{
    var freq, sig;
    // Absolute value boundaries create discontinuous jumps at audio rates
    freq = MouseX.kr(50, 500, 'exponential');
    sig = GbmanSonify.ar(freq);
    Pan2.ar(LeakDC.ar(sig) * 0.1)
}.play;
)
::
